load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A quiver: a directed graph, used as the blueprint for representations, where each node carries a vector space and each
# arrow a linear map. The representation theory of quivers classifies how such diagrams of spaces and maps decompose,
# and it connects to root systems and Lie theory. The form carries the set of nodes.
form quiver
  link nodes, like set
